   "stem": {
      "text": "Let h(x) = x^2 / (x + 3). The line tangent to the graph of h at the point where x = -2 is y = L(x). Which of the following is L(x)?"
   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "symbolic",
      "mathjson": [
         "Add",
         [
            "Multiply",
            -8,
            "x"
         ],
         -12
      ]
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "By the quotient rule, h'(x) = (2x(x + 3) - x^2) / (x + 3)^2 = (x^2 + 6x) / (x + 3)^2.",
         "mathjson": [
            "Divide",
            [
               "Add",
               [
